      "id": "yr42yot",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Lengthiest Written Constitution"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indian Constitution is the lengthiest written constitution in the world, originally containing 395 Articles, 22 Parts, and 8 Schedules.",
        "It establishes a quasi-federal system, blending federal features like division of powers with unitary features like single citizenship and a strong Centre.",
        "Part III guarantees six Fundamental Rights that are justiciable under Article 32.",
        "The 42nd Amendment Act (1976) added 'Secular' to the Preamble and is known as the Mini-Constitution.",
        "The 61st Constitutional Amendment Act (1988) lowered the voting age from 21 to 18 years."
      ],
      "id": "u4supfc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "at2wb6u"
    },
