    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "42nd Amendment Act (1976) is known as the 'Mini-Constitution' and inserted the words Socialist, Secular, and Integrity into the Preamble.",
        "61st Amendment Act (1988) reduced the voting age from 21 to 18 years (effective from 1989).",
        "44th Amendment Act (1978) removed the Right to Property from the list of Fundamental Rights in Part III.",
        "K.C. Wheare described the Constitution of India as 'quasi-federal'."
      ],
